   2290  f750							; ==============================================================================
   2291  f750							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   2292  f750							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   2293  f750							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   2294  f750							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   2295  f750							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   2296  f750							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   2297  f750							;
   2298  f750							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   2299  f750							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   2300  f750							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   2301  f750							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   2302  f750							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   2303  f750							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   2304  f750							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   2305  f750							;
   2306  f750							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   2307  f750							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   2308  f750							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   2309  f750							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   2310  f750							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
